{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:0cf9f8707b1d40b8","name":"Neo-Crusader Marshal","source":{"id":"source:reference-0cf9f8707b1d40b8","title":"Neo-Crusader Marshal","revision":26686,"timestamp":"2025-05-30T04:21:06Z","sha256":"3b7356b59cfe08b402a282bd18127067c089b8cb35a7c5489149faff7850c150","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=26686","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Neo-Crusader%20Marshal&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-0cf9f8707b1d40b8","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Mandalorians"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Mandalorians","referenceId":"reference:b7f4f8a44de3a6c8"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Initially, the golden suits of Marshals are reserved for a handful of Mandalore the Ultimate's closest advisors. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Cassus Fett"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Cassus_Fett","referenceId":"reference:bf3e982ed0e9a09c"}," is one of the earliest to take on the armor, in a show of his support for the color-coded hierarchical system he helps to implement. But even before the assault on ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Old Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Old_Republic","referenceId":"reference:6517b7e15507b001"}," begins, Mandalore has begun to devalue the position, rewarding his personnel vanguard with the gold-colored armor. Soon, issuing the right to wear the golden armor becomes his preferred resolution for a variety of bureaucratic problems.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["As the average quality of the beings in the suits of Marshal armor declines, their powers do not. Marshals exercise command over an amorphous area depending on the proximity of other Marshals; one might command an entire sector, while another directs affairs on only one flank of a battlefield. They are expected to engage in combat personally just as any other Mandalorian, but as the position becomes corrupted near the end of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Mandalorian Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Mandalorian_Wars"},", so, too, do some of the people holding the position; the sight of a Marshal scurrilously issuing orders from a position of safety becomes common.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Neo-Crusader Marshal Statistics (CL 10)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Human"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 3/",{"tag":"a","children":["Noble"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Noble","referenceId":"reference:190d375ec3483f8f"}," 2/",{"tag":"a","children":["Soldier"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Soldier","referenceId":"reference:f826baa05bef6921"}," 4/",{"tag":"a","children":["Officer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Officer","referenceId":"reference:192135a8adabe174"}," 3\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +8; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Low-Light Vision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Low-Light_Vision"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +13\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic, Mando'a\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https:/